    <item>
      <title>Beta 49</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:35:59 +0000</pubDate>
      <link>https://github.com/fogleman/rawr-releases/releases/tag/049-2026.10.25</link>
      <sparkle:version>49</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>Beta 49</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <rawr:sourceCommit>fb636b9abe47f0a3858baa297f50b301d394590b</rawr:sourceCommit>
      <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[
- Raws from many Sony cameras, like the a7R III and IV, the a7 III and the a9, are now sharp at 100%. These cameras store only a small preview in the file, so 100% used to be that preview scaled up. Now rawr develops the raw itself when you zoom in, and on a 60-megapixel camera at 50% too. The first frame can take a second, and its colors may shift a little as it sharpens.
- New: the side rail shows a Source row under Decoded. RAW means rawr developed the raw itself, and Embedded JPEG means you're seeing the picture the camera stored in the file. A few cameras store theirs as Embedded RGB or Embedded HEIF.
- Very long bursts, like thousands of frames grouped into one, are much smoother. Stepping through one no longer beachballs or flashes back to a blurry preview at 100%, and holding Backspace to cycle through one no longer keeps using more memory.
- Cull Bursts on a very long burst finds its picks about three times faster, and the sheet no longer beachballs while the pictures load.
- Align, Score, Cull Bursts and other actions keep running at full speed while rawr's window is behind another app's.
- Aligning a long burst no longer drifts. Over hundreds of frames, a smooth pan could end dozens of pixels off. Now it stays within a few. Bursts you aligned before are measured again the next time you align them.
]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/fogleman/rawr-releases/releases/download/049-2026.10.25/rawr-049-2026.10.25.zip" length="9127974" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="OEF+BwXyPDzh3lQkOKH387ahpigb+3jivdtuugLLEmfI6U3zkiCHA4QDAfNsWEuWW59txyNHKMpuACGqOMjBBw=="></enclosure>
    </item>
